ott around 70-74% to win", "Janoo outraised Scott in September and won Sanders' endorsement"], "rationale": "Scott's durable personal brand has repeatedly let him win in a state with a 17-point Democratic lean, and most expert raters call the race Solid or Likely R while markets put his odds near 70%. The late-September polling is genuinely split, and Janoo's fundraising surge and Sanders endorsement suggest a tightening race, so the forecast sits between the polls and the raters rather than at either extreme.", "watch": "Whether post-endorsement polling in October confirms the UNH tightening or reverts to the double-digit Scott leads shown elsewhere.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Phil Scott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Vermont is one of the most Democratic-leaning states in the country, but Republican Phil Scott has built a durable incumbency through personal popularity and cross-party appeal, and he is seeking another term. Amanda Janoo, a Democrat endorsed by Bernie Sanders in early October, has gained traction: she outraised Scott in September, and polls released in late September show a race that has narrowed considerably.\n\nThe polling picture is inconsistent. A Braun Research survey for Vermont Public put Scott ahead by ten points among likely voters, while a University of New Hampshire survey from the same period showed Janoo slightly ahead. Prediction markets still favor Scott with roughly 70% implied odds, and most expert ratings place the race in the Solid or Likely Republican column. The race appears closer than Scott's past landslides, but he remains the favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2101, "margin": -4.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0165, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0219, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -10.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2344, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2363, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026